
🏛️ Business Understanding & Project Overview
The financial sector is transitioning from static, manual reporting to dynamic, data-driven architectures. This project involved developing a high-performance Power BI suite designed for a finance team to serve a global sales audience. The primary objective was to replace a cumbersome, manual Excel reporting process with a centralized, automated interface.

By establishing a robust semantic layer, the dashboard provides a "single source of truth" for analyzing customer profitability, net interest margins, and credit risk. This enables executives to monitor the health of the portfolio across segments like Business, Syndications, and Real Estate in real-time.

🛠️ Technical Implementation
The solution was built using advanced data engineering and visualization techniques to ensure scalability and depth:

Automated Data Architecture: Leveraged SQL Server as the primary source to feed a star-schema model, replacing manual data entry.

Advanced DAX Logic: Developed complex measures for YOY (Year-Over-Year) comparisons, MTD (Month-to-Date), and YTD (Year-to-Date) tracking.

Income Breakdown Modeling: Implemented Funds Transfer Pricing (FTP) logic to calculate Asset Charges and Credits, providing a realistic view of Net Operating Income.

Risk Integration: Designed a Credit Risk Rating gauge and an Expected Credit Loss (ECL) trend monitor to bridge the gap between profitability and risk.

🔍 Key Insights & Findings
Based on the January 2026 reporting cycle, the dashboard revealed several critical performance trends:

1. Exceptional Profitability Growth
Net Operating Income: Reached $13,233.6K, representing a robust 18.6% YOY increase.

Net Profit: Surged to $8,225.1K, a significant 30.3% growth compared to the previous period.

2. Revenue Drivers & Efficiency
Fee Income: Witnessed a massive 48.1% YOY spike, indicating successful cross-selling and service diversification.

Portfolio Strength: Total Financing Receivables stand at $6,655.2M, with the Business segment contributing the lion's share at $3,353.9M.

3. Margin & Risk Management
Yield vs. Margin: While Business syndications show a healthy 6.2% yield, the Cash Line Facility maintains a higher individual margin of 2.1%.

Risk Monitoring: The ECL Charge hit $754.6K in Jan '26; however, the provision cover remains aligned with the increasing credit risk rating.

🎯 Conclusion
This dashboard represents a successful transition from Associate-level reporting to Executive-level analytics. By automating the interface, the project reduced manual effort for the finance team while providing the sales team with granular, actionable insights into customer profitability. The integration of Microsoft Fabric-ready principles ensures the dashboard is prepared for future enterprise-scale cloud integration.

Final Outcome: An 18.6% increase in Net Operating Income and a 48% growth in Fee Income are now tracked with 100% automation, allowing leadership to focus on strategy rather than data preparation.
